{"styles":[{"sc":"#ff2600","so":1,"w":2,"ol":true,"fc":"#fffb00","fo":0.502}],"cards":["<div style=\"font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;color:#222222;max-width:238px;\"><div style=\"background:#0e7d46;height:6px;border-radius:3px 3px 0 0;\"></div><div style=\"font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.08em;color:#0e7d46;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;padding:7px 0 0;\">COUNTY BOUNDARY</div><div style=\"font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.08em;color:#0e7d46;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;padding:0 0 2px;\">ARIZONA</div><div style=\"font-size:16px;font-weight:800;padding:2px 0 6px;\">Pinal County</div><table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:12px;\"><tr><td style=\"color:#666666;padding:3px 10px 3px 0;white-space:nowrap;\">Population</td><td style=\"color:#111111;font-weight:600;\">539,000 (2025 est.)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#666666;padding:3px 10px 3px 0;white-space:nowrap;\">County Seat</td><td style=\"color:#111111;font-weight:600;\">Florence</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#666666;padding:3px 10px 3px 0;white-space:nowrap;\">Land Area</td><td style=\"color:#111111;font-weight:600;\">5,366 sq mi</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#666666;padding:3px 10px 3px 0;white-space:nowrap;\">Density</td><td style=\"color:#111111;font-weight:600;\">100 / sq mi</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#666666;padding:3px 10px 3px 0;white-space:nowrap;\">Median Household Income</td><td style=\"color:#111111;font-weight:600;\">$80,300</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#666666;padding:3px 10px 3px 0;white-space:nowrap;\">Median Home Value</td><td style=\"color:#111111;font-weight:600;\">$349,000</td></tr></table><div style=\"font-size:12px;line-height:1.55;color:#333333;padding:8px 0 2px;border-top:1px solid #eef2f1;margin-top:7px;\">Pinal County occupies the corridor between metropolitan Phoenix and Tucson and has been one of the fastest-growing counties in the United States, with roughly 539,000 residents spread across Casa Grande, Maricopa, Apache Junction, San Tan Valley and Florence. Much of that growth is master-planned residential development absorbing commuters priced out of both metros, which makes it the most rooftop-driven market in Arizona outside Maricopa County. Manufacturing has become a second pillar as electric-vehicle and battery plants have located along the Interstate 10 corridor, alongside a long-established irrigated agriculture base. Large blocks of state trust land shape where growth can go, so development concentrates along the I-10 and US-60 corridors.</div><div style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888888;padding-top:6px;\">Source: U.S. Census Bureau · Data verified: August 24, 2026</div></div>"],"feats":[["Pinal",0,[[33.46556,-111.15729],[33.46568,-111.06517],[33.46575,-111.03982],[33.43833,-111.02545],[33.42249,-111.01702],[33.39359,-111.00179],[33.39112,-111.00068],[33.37918,-110.99421],[33.37331,-110.9911],[33.36186,-110.98514],[33.34211,-110.97473],[33.31465,-110.96631],[33.25005,-110.94674],[33.23591,-110.93792],[33.16753,-110.8955],[33.16343,-110.89289],[33.11984,-110.86596],[33.11205,-110.86123],[33.0774,-110.83996],[33.04832,-110.82216],[33.0049,-110.79553],[33.00013,-110.79258],[33.00007,-110.79251],[32.98466,-110.78314],[32.98402,-110.78203],[32.98389,-110.78175],[32.98383,-110.78158],[32.98374,-110.78108],[32.98371,-110.78034],[32.98378,-110.77974],[32.98401,-110.7784],[32.98409,-110.77741],[32.98418,-110.77675],[32.9843,-110.77609],[32.98504,-110.77352],[32.98511,-110.77283],[32.98508,-110.77209],[32.98518,-110.77139],[32.98519,-110.77099],[32.98501,-110.76997],[32.98491,-110.76898],[32.98492,-110.76825],[32.98505,-110.76729],[32.98524,-110.76657],[32.98581,-110.76572],[32.98647,-110.76494],[32.98674,-110.7647],[32.98702,-110.76454],[32.98739,-110.76439],[32.98784,-110.76427],[32.98851,-110.76421],[32.98986,-110.76391],[32.9913,-110.7637],[32.99238,-110.76371],[32.99324,-110.76381],[32.99355,-110.76391],[32.99442,-110.76411],[32.99543,-110.76405],[32.99589,-110.76407],[32.99721,-110.76427],[32